Tidy←{
  ⍝ Tidy
  ⍝ Try to align comments nicely in dfn or tradfn source. 
  ⍝ ---------
  ⍝ Syntax: @cvv← [(tab: 65 ⋄ inc: 5  ⋄ min: 15  ⋄ fi: 0 )] ∇ source@cvv|sourceFn@cv 
  ⍝      tab: column in which to put comments if possible.
  ⍝      inc: If text extends to <tab> or beryond, place comments multiples of <inc> 
  ⍝           to the right of position <tab>
  ⍝      min: Keep any comments before column <min> where they are.
  ⍝      fi:  If 1 and ⍵ has depth ≤1, treats ⍵ as the name of a file to update in place (see below).
  ⍝
  ⍝ 1. If source is a char vector of vectors, it is treated as the representation of a function.
  ⍝    a.  Return the source with comments aligned per options. 
  ⍝    b.  The function is NOT refixed-- that's up to you.
  ⍝ 2. If source is a char. vector, and...
  ⍝    a.  if fi is 0, 
  ⍝        - ⍵ refers to the name of a visible function;
  ⍝        - its source representation (verbatim if possible) is formatted and...
  ⍝          - returned as a shy value;
  ⍝    b.  if fi is 1,
  ⍝        - ⍵ refers to a file, which is read;
  ⍝        - its source is formatted and...
  ⍝          - rewritten to the file (in place) and 
  ⍝          - returned as a shy value.
  ⍝ 
    ⎕IO ⎕ML←0 1 
  11 22:: ⎕SIGNAL ⊂⎕DMX.(('EN' EN) ('Message' Message))
    ⍺←() 
    def← (                                                  ⍝ Load the default and user options.
      tab:  60                                          
      inc:   5                                          
      min:  20 
      fi:    0
    )  
    0∊ ⊃∊/(⍺ def).⎕NL ¯2: ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' (∊'Valid options:',' ',¨def.⎕NL ¯2))
    opts← ⎕NS def ⍺ 
  1≥ ≡⍵:  opts ∇ {  
    ~⍺.fi: _← ⍺ ∇ { 
      ~⍵ ⎕NC⍛∊ 3 4: ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message',⍥⊂ '"',⍵,'" is not a fn or op. For files, use option (fi: 1)')
        ⍺ ⍺⍺ 62 ⎕ATX ⍵
      } ⍵
        ⍺.fi← 0 
        ll← ⍺ ⍺⍺ ⊃⎕NGET ⍵ 1
    1:  _← ll⊣ ll ⊂⍛⎕NPUT ⍵ 1  
  } ,⍵      
    Align← { (t i) p← ⍺ ⍵ ⋄ p≤ t: ''⍴⍨ t- p ⋄ ''⍴⍨ i| p- t }
  ⍝ p:    our position on this line.
  ⍝ cs:   If 1, we have seen only comments and spaces on this line.
  ⍝       If 0, we've seen code (incl. guards, quotes, :directives, etc.) on this line. 
  ⍝     
    p cs← 0 1 
    startB codeB cmB spB← ⍳≢pats← ( 
         '^'                                                ⍝ start    (of line)
         '''[^'']*''|[^⍝''\h]+'                             ⍝ code     (fragments)
         '\h*⍝.*$'                                          ⍝ comment  (w/ preceding spaces)
         '\h+'                                              ⍝ spaces   (otherwise)
    )
    pats ⎕R{  
            m← ⍵.Match 
            startB codeB cmB spB← ⍵.PatternNum= ⍳4
          startB: ''⊣ p⊢←0   ⊣ cs⊢← 1                       ⍝ Start of line
          codeB:  m⊣  p+← ≢m ⊣ cs⊢← 0                       ⍝ Code found   
          spB:    m⊣  p+← ≢m                                ⍝ Spaces (not foll by comment)
        ⍝ cmB: code follows...
            nsp← +/ ∧\ m= ' '      
            asis← cs∧ opts.min> p+ nsp                      ⍝ If comment is near start of line (<min), ...
          asis:  m                                          ⍝ ... keep leading spaces
                 m← ' ', nsp↓ m                             ⍝ Not <min, so keep only 1 leading space 
                 m,⍨ opts.(tab inc) Align p+1               ⍝ Align at "next" tab stop (per inc), if >tab already.  
    }⊣⍵
}
